1. Purpose

Grey M1 solver a la Radice et al. 2022 [arXiv:2111.14858].

This code needs 2 ghost cells on unigrid and 4 ghost cells with AMR.

A. Acknowledgements

This code is ported from THC_M1 (https://bitbucket.org/FreeTHC/thccore/src/master/) of Radice et al. 

B. NuRates population-dependent collisions

For rates_lib="NuRates", a local six-variable spectral solve updates all
three evolved species together, with matter/geometry fixed. It recomputes
the population-dependent rates, including inelastic energy redistribution,
at each trial. The existing four-moment source solver supplies the inner
radiation update; analytic limits are starting guesses, not accepted roots.
The scattering-free E-v.F equation and the number/momentum equations are
checked independently. Invalid trials are rejected rather than clamped into
a different distribution. The implementation requires ngroups=1, nspecies=3
and the tabulated EOS; it allocates no diagnostic grid functions.

Scheduled opacities and source trials share unit conversion, equilibrium
targets, exact number-current projection and comoving floor-reference rules.
Heavy-flavor coefficients average neutrino/antineutrino absorption/scattering;
emissivity sums two flavors of each. This matters for asymmetric inelastic
kernels. The temporary floor reference does not modify evolved moments or
the equilibrium conservation budget. Its comoving thresholds deliberately
replace the former lab-floor classification.

Unrestricted source updates retain the accepted root directly. Limited
semi-implicit updates retain the original baseline, so a zero limiter leaves
it unchanged. The source limiter must remain disabled for NuRates IMEX;
numerical post-source repairs are not included in its implicit increment.
WeakRates/FakeRates retain their original source paths.

This solves the configured legacy corrected grey operator, not a fully
coupled matter-radiation system. In particular, the existing separate
electron-flavor Kirchhoff replacements need not preserve pair-only net
electron-neutrino number away from equilibrium. Process-separated treatment
and a pair-only conservation test remain necessary before claiming that
microphysics property. TOV stability and performance require runtime tests;
unit tests alone cannot establish either.
